# ALLOWLIST, not a blocklist.
#
# This repository sits in a folder that also holds real client documents — tax
# returns, bank statements, credit reports. A normal .gitignore lists what to
# exclude and lets everything else through, which means one new file type is all
# it takes to commit a client's SSN into a permanent history.
#
# So: ignore everything, then name the few things that ARE code. Anything not
# named below is invisible to git no matter where it lands.

# 1. ignore everything
*

# 2. but still descend into directories, or the un-ignores below can't match
!*/

# 3. the code and its documentation
!*.py
!*.md
!Cena_5.html
!fq_auditor/assets/review_page.html

!.gitignore

# 4. belt and braces: never these, even if a rule above would allow them
*.pdf
*.PDF
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm
*.csv
*.tsv
*.docx
*.doc
*.pptx
*.qbb
*.qbw
*.qbm
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.eml
*.msg
*.zip
*.json

# 4b. Markdown that is CLIENT DATA rather than documentation.
#
# The audit writes its reports as .md, and those name a real client's banks and
# account tails ("Bank statement · Arvest · x6840"). The allowlist above would
# have committed all of them. A git history is forever, so these stay out.
audit-results/
sample_output/
*Internal Audit.md
*Client Email.md

# NAMING.md, SCORECARD.md, HANDOFF.md and RedactorTest_ANSWER_KEY.md used to be
# excluded here: they illustrate the naming convention, and every example was a
# real client's first name and a real account tail. The examples now use an
# invented household (Hollingsworth — Grant, Nadia, Elise) with invented tails,
# so they are safe to keep. If you add an example, invent it; never paste one
# out of a live client folder.

# 4c. The launcher and its icon. Named individually and placed AFTER the blanket
# rules above, because later rules win — "*.png" further up would otherwise hide
# the icon, and a client's scanned statement is also a .png, which is exactly
# why that blanket rule stays. Anything added here must be named in full: never
# re-open a whole extension.
!*.command
!FQ Toolkit.png

# 4d. The firm's logo, vendored so the app is not dependent on the Analysis
# share being mounted. Named in full for the same reason as the icon above: the
# blanket *.png rule is what keeps clients' scanned statements out of the repo
# and must stay shut.
!fq_auditor/assets/
!fq_auditor/assets/fq_logo.png

# 5. working state, caches, outputs
.fq_cache/
.fq_root
.fq_settings
_Audit/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# 5. the one binary that is code, not client data: the consult deck template,
#    scrubbed of its source client by _spec/build_template.py, which refuses
#    to write it while any of that client survives. Named exactly, so no other
#    .pptx can ride in on this line.
!fq_auditor/assets/consult_template.pptx

# The plugin manifest is code, not client data.
!plugin/fq-prospect/.claude-plugin/plugin.json
